      "id": "df1bb97f-91e8-4072-a841-b0385c478132",
      "name": "DOC 1 - Workflow Details",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        -1104
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 762,
        "height": 977,
        "content": "# Summarize portfolio reviews and flag compliance risk with GPT-4o and Google Sheets\n\n## What this workflow does\nThis workflow automates the operational process represented by **Summarize portfolio reviews and flag compliance risk with GPT-4o and Google Sheets** while keeping decisions, audit records, and notifications traceable.\n\n## Who it is for\nOperations teams, reviewers, and process owners configuring the connected services.\n\n## How it works\n1. **Webhook - Advisor Meeting Notes Form** — Starts the workflow when the configured webhook event occurs.\n2. **Normalize Input** — Normalizes, validates, or reshapes data for the next workflow step.\n3. **OpenAI Chat Model** — Applies the workflow's AI prompt or model to the current business record.\n4. **Structured Output Parser** — Applies the workflow's AI prompt or model to the current business record.\n5. **AI Agent - Summarize & Flag Compliance Risk** — Applies the workflow's AI prompt or model to the current business record.\n6. **Shape Output** — Normalizes, validates, or reshapes data for the next workflow step.\n7. **Log Review to Compliance Tracker** — Reads or writes the operational record in the configured system of record.\n8. **Route by Compliance Risk** — Controls routing, joining, batching, or approval state for this execution.\n9. **Alert Compliance Officer** — Sends the relevant decision, request, or exception to its recipient.\n10. **Send Advisor Summary Email** — Sends the relevant decision, request, or exception to its recipient.\n11. **Alert Compliance Team (High Risk)** — Sends the relevant decision, request, or exception to its recipient.\n\n## Expected result\nA routed, logged, and reviewable operational outcome using the configured integrations."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f11f2bfb-57af-47c8-ada4-78eb3e9df7d8",
      "name": "DOC 2 - Setup Guide",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        -48
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 650,
        "height": 443,
        "content": "# Setup guide\n\n1. Import the workflow JSON into n8n.\n2. Open every node with a warning icon and select the required credential.\n3. Replace placeholder IDs, URLs, recipients, channel IDs, table/sheet names, and thresholds.\n4. Run a manual test using a non-production record.\n5. Confirm each branch, storage write, and notification before activation.\n\n## Credential map\n- **OpenAI Chat Model** → n8n free OpenAI API credits\n\nEstimated setup time: 20–40 minutes."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "eddb025f-acac-4a3d-a764-a1ad3a457c4b",
      "name": "DOC 3 - Customization",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 650,
        "height": 260,
        "content": "# Customization\n\n- Change policy thresholds in Code, If, and Switch nodes.\n- Replace the notification node while preserving its incoming expressions.\n- Add a human approval step before irreversible external actions.\n- Add a second audit sink for reporting or compliance retention.\n- Update AI prompts and schemas for your organization’s terminology."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "7e85902f-6883-454a-beab-03f4c061e01d",
      "name": "DOC 4 - Additional Information",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        800
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 650,
        "height": 420,
        "content": "# Additional information\n\nExternal calls may fail because of credentials, rate limits, or changed API schemas. Review execution logs and enable retries where appropriate.\n\nAI cost depends on model and input length. Minimize personal or confidential data sent to models and stores.\n\nBuilt for local import and first-run verification. Re-check node versions if your n8n release differs materially.\n\nCreator: Swapnil AI Labs — swapnil.mandloi7@gmail.com — swapnilailabs.netlify.app"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
